@page "/guidance"

<PageTitle>Crew guidance | AstroHealth</PageTitle>

<div class="page-heading">
    <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">CREW HEALTH / FIELD NOTES</div>
        <h1>Guidance for the <span class="heading-accent">long haul.</span></h1>
        <p class="page-subtitle">Practical reminders for self-monitoring during a mission.</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="guidance-banner">
    <span class="guidance-mark">!</span>
    <p><strong>This tool does not diagnose or prescribe treatment.</strong> Follow your mission medical officer and established mission protocols, especially if you feel unwell or a reading concerns you.</p>
</div>

<section class="guidance-grid">
    <article class="panel guidance-card">
        <div class="guidance-index">01 / TRACK</div>
        <h2>Build a useful baseline</h2>
        <p>Log measurements consistently and note when they were taken. Trends are more useful than isolated values, but do not replace professional assessment.</p>
        <ul><li>Use the same units each time.</li><li>Record only measurements you can verify.</li><li>Leave unavailable fields blank rather than estimating.</li></ul>
    </article>
    <article class="panel guidance-card">
        <div class="guidance-index">02 / RECOVER</div>
        <h2>Protect rest and routine</h2>
        <p>Sleep, mood, activity, and connection with crewmates are part of overall wellbeing in confined environments.</p>
        <ul><li>Keep a regular sleep schedule when mission operations allow.</li><li>Report persistent sleep or mood changes early.</li><li>Use scheduled exercise and recovery plans.</li></ul>
    </article>
    <article class="panel guidance-card">
        <div class="guidance-index">03 / RESPOND</div>
        <h2>Escalate concerns</h2>
        <p>A status label is a prompt to review, not a medical conclusion. Symptoms and mission protocols always take priority over an app.</p>
        <ul><li>Contact the crew medical officer about concerning symptoms.</li><li>Follow established emergency communication procedures.</li><li>Do not change medication or treatment based on this dashboard.</li></ul>
    </article>
</section>

<div class="guidance-footnote">Monitoring thresholds in this prototype are illustrative and require validation by qualified aerospace medical professionals before operational use.</div>
